## Project Overview
Bar management system for small-to-medium counter bars in Thailand.
NestJS modular monolith — REST API + WebSocket gateway + webhook receiver in one process.
2 developers. Senior capstone project, DPU Computer Engineering. Deadline: April 2027.
AI integration (OpenAI) for guest preference summary only — not a chat AI.

## Tech Stack
- Runtime:     Node.js 22, ESM (type: "module"), TypeScript 6
- Framework:   NestJS 12 — ports & adapters (hexagonal) architecture
- Database:    PostgreSQL, TypeORM — synchronize: false always
- Cache:       Redis (ElastiCache) — ACL + session + BullMQ + WebSocket pub/sub
- Queue:       BullMQ (@nestjs/bullmq) — backed by Redis
- WebSocket:   NestJS Gateway (socket.io + Redis adapter)
- Auth:        LINE SSO + JWT + refresh token rotation
- Payment:     PromptPay QR + GB Prime Pay webhook
- AI:          OpenAI API (guest preference summary — Semester 2)
- Infra:       AWS ECS/ECR + RDS + S3 + ElastiCache
- Local dev:   Docker Compose (Postgres + Redis) + ngrok

## ESM Import Rules
- Module resolution: NodeNext — relative imports MUST use .js extension
  even though the source file is .ts
  ✅ import { Foo } from './foo.service.js'
  ❌ import { Foo } from './foo.service'
- Node built-ins: import { randomUUID } from 'node:crypto'
- Package imports: no extension needed (import { Injectable } from '@nestjs/common')

## Architecture: Hexagonal (Ports & Adapters)

### Layers (strict — never import upward or across)
1. domain/ports/    → interfaces only. No framework imports. No TypeORM.
2. application/     → service classes, use cases. Imports ports, not adapters.
3. infrastructure/  → adapters. Implements ports. Imports frameworks (TypeORM, Redis, etc.)
4. common/          → shared kernel. No business logic. No domain imports.

### Rule: application/ NEVER imports from infrastructure/
Services receive ports via constructor injection.
The NestJS module wires the concrete adapter to the port token.

### Port naming convention
- Interface file:          [entity].repository.port.ts
- Interface name:          I[Entity]Repository
- DI injection token:      [ENTITY]_REPOSITORY (symbol or string)
- Adapter implements:      class [Entity]TypeOrmRepository implements I[Entity]Repository

