## BaseEntity
File: common/base/base.entity.ts
All mutable entities extend BaseEntity. Never repeat these columns.
- id:         UUID PK (@PrimaryGeneratedColumn('uuid'))
- createdBy:  UUID FK → staff_user (nullable)
- updatedBy:  UUID FK → staff_user (nullable)
- createdAt:  timestamptz, default NOW()
- updatedAt:  timestamptz, default NOW()

AuditLog does NOT extend BaseEntity — it has its own schema.
BaseEntity FK columns are populated automatically by AuditSubscriber via @nestjs/cls.
Never manually set createdBy / updatedBy in service code.

## Column Type Constants
File: common/constants/sql-column.constant.ts
No magic strings for column types anywhere in the codebase.
Always import and use named constants:
export const COL = {
  UUID:       { type: 'uuid' },
  VARCHAR200: { type: 'varchar', length: 200 },
  VARCHAR100: { type: 'varchar', length: 100 },
  TEXT:       { type: 'text' },
  BOOL:       { type: 'boolean' },
  NUMERIC102: { type: 'numeric', precision: 10, scale: 2 },
  NUMERIC123: { type: 'numeric', precision: 12, scale: 3 },
  TIMESTAMPTZ:{ type: 'timestamptz' },
  JSONB:      { type: 'jsonb' },
  SMALLINT:   { type: 'smallint' },
} as const;

## TypeORM Rules
- synchronize: false — always, no exceptions
- No eager: true on any relation
- Always @JoinColumn({ name: 'snake_case_column_name' }) on the owning (@ManyToOne) side
- camelCase properties; TypeORM maps to snake_case via SnakeNamingStrategy
- Nullable FK: { nullable: true } on both @Column and @ManyToOne
- Relations loaded explicitly via relations: {} in queries — never auto-loaded
- All relations declare both sides: @ManyToOne on child, @OneToMany on parent
- No @Exclude() on entities — mapper functions handle response shaping
- namingStrategy: SnakeNamingStrategy from typeorm-naming-strategies
- Use save() not update() on all audited entities — AuditSubscriber needs databaseEntity
- All queries filter deletedOn: IsNull() unless explicitly fetching deleted records
- SSL: enabled when NODE_ENV !== 'local' — { rejectUnauthorized: false }

## Entity Injection Token Pattern
Every port has a Symbol token in the same file.
The module binds the TypeORM adapter to that token.

// staff-user.repository.port.ts
export const STAFF_USER_REPOSITORY = Symbol('STAFF_USER_REPOSITORY');
export interface IStaffUserRepository { ... }

// iam.module.ts
providers: [
  { provide: STAFF_USER_REPOSITORY, useClass: StaffUserTypeOrmRepository },
  StaffUserService,  // receives IStaffUserRepository via @Inject(STAFF_USER_REPOSITORY)
]

## DTO Pattern
- Zod schemas for all DTOs — inferred TypeScript types, NOT classes
- DTOs are plain types: export type CreateOrderDto = z.infer<typeof CreateOrderSchema>
- Use plain mapper functions (toOrderDto, toOrderItemDto) for entity → response shape
- Do NOT use class-based DTOs with static from() methods
- Controller owns response shape — calls mapper after service returns entity
- No class-validator / class-transformer on DTOs

## IAM & Permissions
- permission format: 'resource:action' e.g. 'orders:create', 'menu:manage'
- @RequirePermissions('orders:create') on controller methods
- PermissionsGuard (in common/) resolves the current user's effective permissions:
  1. Load group memberships where NOW() BETWEEN valid_from AND valid_until (or valid_until IS NULL)
  2. Union of all group policies + direct user policies → union of all permissions
  3. Cache result in Redis key: `acl:{userId}` with short TTL
  4. Invalidate on ANY IAM change (group membership, policy assignment)
- permission-resolver.service.ts in IamModule — exported so AuthModule can use it
- PermissionsGuard in CommonModule — imports IamModule to call permission-resolver
- Never inline permission checks in service code — always go through the guard

## Auth Pattern (LINE SSO)
- LINE Login callback → exchange code → get LINE profile → upsert staff_user_identity
- Issue JWT access token (short-lived) + refresh token (long-lived, stored in HttpOnly cookie)
- Refresh rotation: old refresh token invalidated on use
- JWT payload: { sub: staffUserId, venueId }
- @CurrentUser() decorator extracts JWT payload from request

## BullMQ Pattern (PaymentModule)
- Queue name: 'payments'
- Webhook controller: validate → check gateway_tx_id idempotency → enqueue job → return 200 fast
- Processor (payment.processor.ts): dequeue → update payment status → emit WebSocket event
- Idempotency: SELECT payment WHERE gateway_tx_id = $1 before processing
- Race condition: pessimistic lock (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE) on visit row when creating payment
  ConflictException if PENDING payment already exists for that visit
- Never delete failed jobs — let BullMQ retry with backoff
- Processor lives in infrastructure/queue/ inside PaymentModule — not a separate module

## WebSocket Pattern (NotificationsModule)
- NotificationsGateway: socket.io adapter, manages room subscriptions
- NotificationsService: injectable by OrderModule, PaymentModule — emits events
- Rooms: 'pos' | 'bar-display' | 'kitchen-display'
- Multi-instance: Redis adapter (socket.io-redis) bridges ECS tasks
- Never import NotificationsGateway directly into domain modules — import NotificationsService
- OrderModule → NotificationsService.emitOrderUpdate(room, payload)
- PaymentModule → NotificationsService.emitPaymentUpdate(room, payload)

## Transaction Management
- @nestjs-cls/transactional + @nestjs-cls/transactional-adapter-typeorm
- @Transactional() decorator on service methods that span multiple repos
- Never manually pass EntityManager to repository methods
- Payment status update to FAILED always runs OUTSIDE transaction
  (must persist even when transaction rolls back)

## Config Pattern
- ConfigModule.forRoot() in AppModule only
- ConfigModule.forFeature(registerAs('domain', () => ({...}))) per module
- Each domain config has its own typed wrapper class
- All reads from process.env — source is irrelevant to the app
- registerAs domains:
  'database'  → DB_HOST, DB_PORT, DB_USER, DB_PASS, DB_NAME
  'redis'     → REDIS_HOST, REDIS_PORT, REDIS_PASSWORD
  'auth'      → LINE_CLIENT_ID, LINE_CLIENT_SECRET, LINE_CALLBACK_URL
  'jwt'       → JWT_SECRET, JWT_EXPIRES_IN, REFRESH_TOKEN_SECRET, REFRESH_TOKEN_EXPIRES_IN
  'payment'   → GB_PRIME_SECRET, GB_PRIME_PUBLIC_KEY
  'openai'    → OPENAI_API_KEY, OPENAI_MODEL (Semester 2)

## Environment Convention
NODE_ENV=local       → developer machine, Docker Compose, no SSL
NODE_ENV=development → shared dev, RDS dev, SSL enabled
NODE_ENV=production  → live, RDS prod, SSL enabled
SSL: enabled when NODE_ENV !== 'local'

## Module Rules
- Feature modules export their Service, never their Repository
- Never share a repository across modules — share the service instead
- Domain modules import other domain modules when they need their service
- IamModule exports PermissionResolverService (used by CommonModule's guard)
- NotificationsModule exported globally — import once in AppModule
- Audit log has no module — AuditSubscriber in CommonModule handles it globally

## AuditSubscriber Rules
- Registered once in AppModule via DataSource event subscriber
- Listens to afterInsert + afterUpdate on all entities extending BaseEntity
- Reads current staff user from @nestjs/cls context (set by JWT middleware)
- Skips audit meta-fields: createdBy, updatedBy, createdAt, updatedAt
- diff format: { fieldName: { from: oldVal, to: newVal } } — scalar fields only
- audit_log is append-only: never UPDATE or DELETE it

## Critical Domain Rules
- price snapshots: order_item.unit_price_snapshot frozen at order time
  Menu price changes NEVER affect existing orders
- payment idempotency: always check gateway_tx_id uniqueness before processing webhook
- visit state machine: open → closed | abandoned. Never reopen a closed visit.
  VistService owns state transitions — no direct state mutation elsewhere
- bottle-keep is NOT inventory: already sold to customer. No inventory deduction on pour.
- menu_variant_ingredient lives in MenuModule (recipe definition)
  InventoryModule receives deduction calls from OrderModule — it never reads menu tables
- kitchen_display_enabled stored in venue table (not env var) — admin toggles at runtime
- PDPA: customer_id on visit is nullable — linked post-hoc with explicit consent only
  AI summarizes preferences only — never behavioral judgment, never identity inference

## Shared Types (@bar/contracts)
- Import shared enums from '@bar/contracts' in both frontend and backend
- OrderStatus, PaymentStatus, SessionState, StaffRole already defined
- Add new shared types to packages/contracts/src/ as domains are built

## Soft Delete
- Never hard delete any record
- Soft delete: deletedAt timestamptz + deletedBy UUID on the entity
  (add to individual entities that need it, not to BaseEntity)
- Always filter deletedAt: IsNull() on active record queries

## What NOT To Do
- Do NOT use synchronize: true
- Do NOT use eager: true on relations
- Do NOT return raw TypeORM entities from controllers — always map to DTO
- Do NOT import infrastructure/ from application/ layer
- Do NOT import from another module's infrastructure/ directly — use exported service
- Do NOT inline permission checks in services — use @RequirePermissions() guard
- Do NOT use update() on audited entities — use save()
- Do NOT hard delete records
- Do NOT store magic strings for column types — use COL constants
- Do NOT repeat audit columns on individual entities — extend BaseEntity
- Do NOT add id to individual entities — inherited from BaseEntity
- Do NOT put business logic in repositories — repositories are data access only
- Do NOT share repositories across modules
- Do NOT export repositories from feature modules
- Do NOT resolve FK codes to IDs inside repositories — service does that
- Do NOT touch audit_log with UPDATE or DELETE — append only
- Do NOT reopen a closed visit
- Do NOT modify order_item.unit_price_snapshot after creation
- Do NOT process a payment webhook without checking gateway_tx_id idempotency
- Do NOT build kitchen display UI in Semester 1 — routing logic yes, UI no
- Do NOT add offline mode, member QR, staff performance analytics (cut from scope)
- Do NOT add Kubernetes/EKS until ECS is stable and shipped
- Do NOT expand scope — finish order → pay → close first
- Do NOT omit .js extensions on relative imports (ESM NodeNext rule)
